======================================================================
DISCOVERY: The v_2 staircase
======================================================================

At fixed d, v_2(M_amp(n,d,0)) = -d - s_2(n-2-d) depends on n through s_2.

s_2(m) has a fractal structure:
  m = 0: s_2 = 0
  m = 1: s_2 = 1
  m = 2: s_2 = 1
  m = 3: s_2 = 2
  m = 4: s_2 = 1
  m = 5: s_2 = 2
  m = 6: s_2 = 2
  m = 7: s_2 = 3
  m = 8: s_2 = 1

At d=1: v_2 = -1 - s_2(n-3). The MINIMUM v_2 (most 2-adic precision)
occurs when s_2(n-3) is maximized, i.e., n-3 = 2^k - 1 (all 1s in binary).
  n = 4: v_2 = -2 (n-3=1, s_2=1)
  n = 6: v_2 = -3 (n-3=3, s_2=2)  <-- n=6 AGAIN!
  n = 10: v_2 = -4 (n-3=7, s_2=3)
  n = 18: v_2 = -5 (n-3=15, s_2=4)

The n where v_2(d=1) is MOST negative is n = 2^k + 3:
  n = 4, 6, 10, 18, 34, 66, ...

These are the LEAST universal n for the signed HP permanent!

Least-universal n (s_2(n-3) maximized for each bit-length):
  n=4: n-3=1=0b1, s_2=1, v_2(d=1)=-2
  n=6: n-3=3=0b11, s_2=2, v_2(d=1)=-3
  n=10: n-3=7=0b111, s_2=3, v_2(d=1)=-4
  n=18: n-3=15=0b1111, s_2=4, v_2(d=1)=-5
  n=34: n-3=31=0b11111, s_2=5, v_2(d=1)=-6
  n=66: n-3=63=0b111111, s_2=6, v_2(d=1)=-7
  n=130: n-3=127=0b1111111, s_2=7, v_2(d=1)=-8
  n=258: n-3=255=0b11111111, s_2=8, v_2(d=1)=-9
  n=514: n-3=511=0b111111111, s_2=9, v_2(d=1)=-10

